{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\n`o` opens an item in the browser, but often the URL itself is what you want — to paste into a chat, an issue or a commit message. The clipboard plumbing already exists (`PaneEvent::CopyToClipboard`, used by the git log's `y` hash copy), so add a \"copy URL\" action everywhere a URL can be opened.\n\n## Spec\n\n- `y` copies the selected item's URL to the clipboard and shows `Copied <url>` in the status bar:\n  - **GitHub page** — issue list / PR list / Workflow Runs list (and while their detail views are shown)\n  - **Projects page** — board / table items (issues and PRs copy their own URL, drafts the project URL) and the optional `projects` list pane (the project URL)\n  - **Git page** (`git_log`) — `y` is taken by the hash copy, so `Y` copies the commit's GitHub URL\n- URLs are built **locally**, exactly like `o` (PR #141's `parse_github_nwo`) — no API calls. On a non-GitHub remote the status bar says so instead.\n- Uses the existing clipboard mechanism; nothing about the read-only concept changes (no system state is touched).\n\n## Docs / demo\n\n- README en/ja and the guide's GitHub / Projects / Git chapters: add `y` (`Y`) to the key tables; update the Config Reference action lists.\n- Add one `y` moment to the existing GitHub view tape and re-record.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-03T05:30:54Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":156,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Copy the URL of anything o can open in the browser"}
